#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:5
msgid "Configuring setuptools using ``setup.cfg`` files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:7
msgid "New in 30.3.0 (8 Dec 2016)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:10
msgid ""
"If compatibility with legacy builds (i.e. those not using the :pep:`517` "
"build API) is desired, a ``setup.py`` file containing a ``setup()`` function "
"call is still required even if your configuration resides in ``setup.cfg``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:14
msgid ""
"``Setuptools`` allows using configuration files (for example, :file:`setup."
"cfg`) to define a package’s metadata and other options (declarative config)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:17
msgid ""
"This approach allows automation scenarios and can reduce boilerplate code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:21
msgid ""
"[metadata]\n"
"name = my_package\n"
"version = attr: my_package.VERSION\n"
"author = Josiah Carberry\n"
"author_email = josiah_carberry@brown.edu\n"
"description = My package description\n"
"long_description = file: README.rst, CHANGELOG.rst, LICENSE.rst\n"
"keywords = one, two\n"
"license = BSD-3-Clause\n"
"classifiers =\n"
"    Framework :: Django\n"
"    Programming Language :: Python :: 3\n"
"\n"
"[options]\n"
"zip_safe = False\n"
"include_package_data = True\n"
"packages = find:\n"
"python_requires = >=3.8\n"
"install_requires =\n"
"    requests\n"
"    importlib-metadata; python_version<\"3.10\"\n"
"\n"
"[options.package_data]\n"
"* = *.txt, *.rst\n"
"hello = *.msg\n"
"\n"
"[options.entry_points]\n"
"console_scripts =\n"
"    executable-name = my_package.module:function\n"
"\n"
"[options.extras_require]\n"
"pdf = ReportLab>=1.2; RXP\n"
"rest = docutils>=0.3; pack ==1.1, ==1.3\n"
"\n"
"[options.packages.find]\n"
"exclude =\n"
"    examples*\n"
"    tools*\n"
"    docs*\n"
"    my_package.tests*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:64
msgid "Metadata and options are set in the config sections of the same name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:66
msgid ""
"Keys are the same as the :doc:`keyword arguments </references/keywords>` one "
"provides to the ``setup()`` function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:69
msgid ""
"Complex values can be written comma-separated or placed one per line in "
"*dangling* config values. The following are equivalent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:72
msgid ""
"[metadata]\n"
"keywords = one, two\n"
"\n"
"[metadata]\n"
"keywords =\n"
"    one\n"
"    two"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:82
msgid ""
"In some cases, complex values can be provided in dedicated subsections for "
"clarity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:85
msgid ""
"Some keys allow ``file:``, ``attr:``, ``find:``, and ``find_namespace:`` "
"directives in order to cover common usecases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:88
msgid "Unknown keys are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:92
msgid "Using a ``src/`` layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:94
msgid ""
"One commonly used configuration has all the Python source code in a "
"subdirectory (often called the ``src/`` layout), like this::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:97
msgid ""
"├── src\n"
"│   └── mypackage\n"
"│       ├── __init__.py\n"
"│       └── mod1.py\n"
"├── setup.py\n"
"└── setup.cfg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:104
msgid ""
"You can set up your ``setup.cfg`` to automatically find all your packages in "
"the subdirectory, using :ref:`package_dir <keyword/package_dir>`, like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:107
msgid ""
"# This example contains just the necessary options for a src-layout, set up\n"
"# the rest of the file as described above.\n"
"\n"
"[options]\n"
"package_dir=\n"
"    =src\n"
"packages=find:\n"
"\n"
"[options.packages.find]\n"
"where=src"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:120
msgid ""
"In this example, the value for the :ref:`package_dir <keyword/package_dir>` "
"configuration (i.e. ``=src``) is parsed as ``{\"\": \"src\"}``. The ``\"\"`` "
"key has a special meaning in this context, and indicates that all the "
"packages are contained inside the given directory. Also note that the value "
"for ``[options.packages.find] where`` matches the value associated with "
"``\"\"`` in the ``package_dir`` dictionary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:137
msgid "Interpolation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:139
msgid ""
"Config files are parsed using :mod:`configparser` with `interpolation "
"<https://docs.python.org/3/library/configparser.html#interpolation-of-"
"values>`_ enabled. As a result, one config value may reference another. This "
"feature may be used, for example, in defining extras:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:144
msgid ""
"[options.extras_require]\n"
"tester =\n"
"    pytest==3.3.2\n"
"    pytest-sugar\n"
"dev =\n"
"    pytest-xdist\n"
"    %(tester)s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:155
msgid "Specifying values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:157
msgid "Some values are treated as simple strings, some allow more logic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:159
msgid "Type names used below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:161
msgid "``str`` - simple string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:162
msgid "``list-comma`` - dangling list or string of comma-separated values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:163
msgid "``list-semi`` - dangling list or string of semicolon-separated values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:164
msgid "``bool`` - ``True`` is 1, yes, true"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:165
msgid ""
"``dict`` - list-comma where each entry corresponds to a key/value pair, with "
"keys separated from values by ``=``. If an entry starts with ``=``, the key "
"is assumed to be an empty string (e.g. ``=src`` is parsed as ``{\"\": "
"\"src\"}``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:169
msgid "``section`` - values are read from a dedicated (sub)section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:172
msgid "Special directives:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:174
msgid "``attr:`` - Value is read from a module attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:176
msgid ""
"It is advisable to use literal values together with ``attr:`` (e.g. ``str``, "
"``tuple[str]``, see :func:`ast.literal_eval`). This is recommend in order to "
"support the common case of a literal value assigned to a variable in a "
"module containing (directly or indirectly) third-party imports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:181
msgid ""
"``attr:`` first tries to read the value from the module by examining the "
"module's AST.  If that fails, ``attr:`` falls back to importing the module, "
"using :func:`importlib.util.spec_from_file_location` recommended recipe "
"(see :ref:`example on Python docs <python:importlib-examples>` about "
"\"Importing a source file directly\"). Note however that importing the "
"module is error prone since your package is not installed yet. You may also "
"need to manually add the project directory to ``sys.path`` (via ``setup."
"py``) in order to be able to do that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:190
msgid ""
"When the module is imported, ``attr:`` supports callables and iterables; "
"unsupported types are cast using ``str()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:194
msgid "``file:`` - Value is read from a list of files and then concatenated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:197
msgid ""
"The ``file:`` directive is sandboxed and won't reach anything outside the "
"project directory (i.e. the directory containing ``setup.cfg``/``pyproject."
"toml``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:201
msgid ""
"If you are using an old version of ``setuptools``, you might need to ensure "
"that all files referenced by the ``file:`` directive are included in the "
"``sdist`` (you can do that via ``MANIFEST.in`` or using plugins such as "
"``setuptools-scm``, please have a look on :doc:`/userguide/miscellaneous` "
"for more information)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/declarative_config.rst:206
msgid ""
"Newer versions of ``setuptools`` will automatically add these files to the "
"``sdist``."
msgstr ""

